  "alphanli_exclusion": "\u03b1NLI is a different task. The input is an observation-start, two hypotheses, and an observation-end, and the label is which hypothesis better explains the transition \u2014 a 2-way abductive choice. SNLI and MNLI are 3-way entailment / neutral / contradiction on one premise\u2013hypothesis pair. Entropy is not on the same scale (the maximum is log2(2) = 1 for \u03b1NLI and log2(3) \u2248 1.585 for SNLI/MNLI), and one argmax accuracy would mix two decision problems. ChaosNLI-\u03b1 (1,532 items) is excluded. The population is the SNLI subset (1,514) plus the MNLI-matched subset (1,599), 3,113 items.",
